<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So my concern here is that you're trying to put too many historical events together without something that connects them directly. At this moment, this seems like a historical lesson with a 'funny' character to explain it, like a documentary for kids or something. I would suggest to pick only one event and focus on it. Maybe the demon had something to do with it? Maybe its obsession with shoes comes from something that happen in that event?</p>
<p>Also, I feel like the anomaly isn't interesting on its own. Like, the only backstory it hs is regarding human history, and all of its abilities feel like they're just there so it can travel through history without being noticed. Again, this feels like a documentary for kids. Also, I agree with JamaisJ's point about the Foundation having better sources.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I think you should choose just one historical event and then make your anomaly to interact with it.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>

