<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>personnel are to be deterred from ingesting</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why? What happens when you eat it? Sure, it has healing properties, but why should they stop the personnel from eating it <em>at all costs</em>? How long do these properties last? You should explain them more in-depth.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>one instance is recovered by a researcher and a containment engineer.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why did they send a researcher and an engineer? Wouldn't it be best to send and MTF? I suggest to change this to either two MTF members or that the researcher and the engineer got trapped during the storm and they're waiting for rescue.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>but the researcher had consumed the herb prior to death</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why did he do so? Didn't the herb help him to recover? Why did he wish to be cremated if he had already consumed the herb? I really feel like this part is just here to eventually get to the dissection scene. And I feel like the dissection scene is just there to shock the reader without too much effort.</p>
<p>I would suggest to change the anomaly's properties so they have something to do with 'survival'. That way you could add some arguments between the two regarding if they should use the anomaly or not. Also, some personal drama would help a lot in this concept.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I like this concept, but I think you should focus on the struggle to survive rather than trying to shock the reader.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look!</p>

							</div>

								
					
